// Type effectiveness chart — docs/02-GAME-DESIGN.md §1. The table there is law.
//
// Fully explicit 12×12: every attacker lists every defender, in canonical
// type order, so the validator proves totality instead of assuming neutral
// for gaps (doc 04 §3 rule 6). `tools validate` and the cross-transcription
// test in crates/data/tests/core_content.rs must stay green when editing.
//
// Doc note: doc 02 §1's derived-weakness sanity line originally said
// frost 3; corrected to 4 in the doc changelog (2026-06-10) — the table
// (ember, stone, alloy, resonant all hit frost 2×) was always the truth.
TypeChart(
    entries: {
        Feral: {
            Feral: Neutral, Ember: Neutral, Tide: Neutral, Bloom: Neutral,
            Volt: Neutral, Gale: Neutral, Stone: Half, Frost: Neutral,
            Venom: Neutral, Phantom: Zero, Alloy: Half, Resonant: Neutral,
        },
        Ember: {
